{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nRead a personal, **gitignored-by-convention** `.vig.kdl` from the current worktree root and merge it on top of the user config. Full config schema (same as the user config — theme, icons, `pages`, `projects-board`, `app { }`, page layouts and keys); it is the user's own file, so nothing is restricted.\n\nBecause a cloned repository may *ship* a committed `.vig.kdl`, trust is decided by git tracking:\n\n- **Untracked** `.vig.kdl` → the user's own file → loaded silently.\n- **Tracked** `.vig.kdl` → repo-provided → a **trust dialog** on startup (before the app is built, since config affects pages and keybindings):\n  - `[y]` load and remember, `[n]` ignore and remember, `[v]` view the file, then decide\n  - The decision is stored in `~/.local/state/vig/trust.json` (XDG state dir) keyed by **(worktree path, file content hash)** — when the file changes (e.g. on pull), the dialog is shown again. Decisions are per content, deliberately stricter than a per-folder trust.\n  - `vig config trust` lists remembered decisions; `vig config trust --forget <path>` removes one.\n\n## Spec\n\n- Merge order: builtin → user → repo-local (repo-local wins). `--config` / `$VIG_CONFIG` replace the user layer only.\n- Kill switch: `repo-config \"off\"` in the user config disables the repo layer entirely (no dialog either). Default `\"on\"`.\n- Errors in `.vig.kdl` (parse/validation) do **not** abort: vig starts with builtin + user and shows `ignored .vig.kdl: <summary>` in the status bar (one line on stderr too). User-config errors stay fail-fast as today.\n- Visibility: `vig config path` becomes a layer listing (builtin / user / repo-local with path and loaded / ignored+reason); on startup the status bar shows `loaded .vig.kdl` once.\n- Worktrees: the current worktree's root is consulted.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Repo-layer discovery + tracked/untracked detection (`git ls-files`) + merge wiring in `config::source`\n- [ ] Trust store (state dir, JSON, content hash) + pre-app trust dialog (y / n / v) + `vig config trust [--forget <path>]`\n- [ ] `repo-config` user-config node (kill switch) + validation\n- [ ] Non-fatal repo-layer errors (status-bar notice) — user layer unchanged\n- [ ] `vig config path` layer listing; startup `loaded .vig.kdl` notice\n- [ ] docs/config.md (layering, trust model), README (short mention), tests (layer precedence, tracked vs untracked, trust store roundtrip, hash invalidation, kill switch, error degradation)\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T03:58:07Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":132,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Repository-local personal config (.vig.kdl) with a trust dialog for tracked files"}
